# Hydroponic lettuce sensor dataset — built from HydroGrowNet EXP.1/2/3

Source: HydroGrowNet of Batavia Dataset, Mendeley Data,
DOI [10.17632/g6cm3v3wdp.5](https://doi.org/10.17632/g6cm3v3wdp.5).
NFT hydroponic system, Batavia lettuce (*Lactuca sativa* L.),
Arab Academy for Science, Technology and Maritime Transport.
Three 30-day experiments, 10 March – 19 June 2024.

## Files

| File | Rows | What it is |
|---|---|---|
| `hydroponic_lettuce_full.csv` | 726 | Every water-quality reading, joined with air data and labelled |
| `hydroponic_lettuce_train.csv` | 1680 | Training split, class-balanced by oversampling |
| `hydroponic_lettuce_test.csv` | 162 | Test split, real distribution, never resampled |
| `hydroponic_air_hourly.csv` | 2069 | The hourly air logger series on its own |
| `build_dataset.py` | — | Rebuilds everything from the three workbooks |
| `train_model.py` | — | Starter Random Forest for both tasks |

## Where the numbers come from

Each workbook has six sheets. Only two carry sensor data:

- **`Water quality measurments Senso`** — despite the name, the pH / EC / TDS /
  water-temperature columns are **headers with no data in all three workbooks**.
  What is populated is an hourly air logger: RH %, air temperature, CO2 ppm.
  641 + 718 + 712 = 2069 usable rows. These are the "600+ records" you saw.
- **`Water quality parametersPortabl`** — handheld meter readings, twice a day
  (10:00 and 14:00) for six replicate tanks (R1–R3 × T1/T2): pH, EC, TDS, water
  temperature, plus Lux / RH / air temperature. 726 valid readings.

The remaining sheets (`Seedlings measurements`, `Head diameter`,
`Harvest measurements`, `Nutrients Water consumptions`, `Test Taste`) hold plant
growth and tasting data, not sensor readings, so they are not used here.

**726 is the true ceiling for rows containing pH and EC.** Joining hourly air to
water readings would give ~12,000 rows, but each pH value would repeat 24 times
per day. That inflates size without adding information and makes any model look
better than it is, so it is not done.

## Corrections applied — no sensor value was changed

1. **Dates**: the portable sheet stores day and month swapped (`2024-10-03`
   where the experiment window proves 10 March 2024). Swapped back.
2. **Column order**: RH and air temperature sit in different positions in each
   workbook, and EXP.2's 14:00 block has a header that contradicts its own
   values. Reassigned by reading the header, then by value where the header is
   wrong. Without this you get 60 °C "air temperature".
3. **Sensor faults**: one pH of 2.0 and one EC of 26.7 are physically
   impossible. Blanked to missing — never replaced with a different number.

Everything else is exactly as recorded.

